#: ../../reference/config.rst:4
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:6
msgid ""
"A node reads its configuration from ``config.json`` in its data "
"directory. A hub reads command-line flags and, for federation, "
"``federation.json`` in its data directory. This page lists every key, its"
" default and the way to change it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:10
msgid ""
"The configuration has few keys on purpose. A key exists only when someone"
" needs a value other than the default and the value cannot be derived "
"from other information. Internal timings, limits that form a security "
"boundary and the location of files inside the data directory are "
"constants and not settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:21
msgid "How the configuration is changed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:23
msgid ""
"``anet init`` writes the defaults and never changes a value that is "
"already set. Three rules govern the entry points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:26
msgid ""
"A key that changes trust, spending or identity is changed only through "
"the command line, and the command asks for confirmation on the terminal. "
"Without a terminal it refuses with ``tty_required``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:29
msgid ""
"Every other key is edited in ``config.json``. The daemon reads the file "
"when it starts, so a change takes effect after a restart. A key that has "
"a command takes effect at once when it is set through that command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:32
msgid "The MCP tools never change the configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:34
msgid ""
"The daemon refuses to start when ``config.json`` contains a removed key, "
"and prints the sentence ``config_key_removed`` with the replacement (:ref"
":`reference-config-removed`). It also refuses to start when a value fails"
" validation (``config_invalid``). ``anet doctor`` reports removed keys "
"under ``config.removed`` before the daemon is started."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:45
msgid ""
"A complete minimal ``config.json`` after a join looks as follows. Keys "
"that have their default value need not appear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:60
msgid ""
"The port in ``control_addr`` is an example. ``anet id new`` assigns a "
"free port."
msgstr ""

