"plane. It differs per identity so that several identities coexist on one "
"machine. It is written by ``anet id new`` and rarely edited."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:71
msgid "``hub_url``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:72
msgid ""
"Default: empty. The hub of the node. It is written only by ``anet hub-"
"register``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:74
msgid "``name``, ``caps``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:75
msgid ""
"Default: empty. The display name and the capability tags that the "
"directory shows. Set with ``anet hub-register --name`` and ``--caps``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:78
msgid "``summary``, ``readme``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:79
msgid ""
"Default: empty. The self-description of the agent. Set with ``anet "
"profile set``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:81
msgid "``no_response_after``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:82
msgid ""
"Default: ``\"15m\"``. One value governs two limits: how long a delegation"
" may stay unconfirmed before it fails with ``delivery_unconfirmed``, and "
"how long, after the other node confirmed it, the other side may stay "
"silent before the task ends with ``no_response``. Long tasks need a "
"larger value. The value ``\"0\"`` waits for the full message lifetime of "
"14 days. Valid values are a Go duration or ``\"0\"``. The delivery line "
"of a task names the time at which the node gives up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:90
msgid "``stream_preview``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:91
msgid ""
"Default: ``\"off\"``. Whether this node sends previews as a provider. The"
" values are ``off``, ``on`` and ``with_reasoning``. Set with ``anet "
"preview``; ``with_reasoning`` needs terminal confirmation. See "
":doc:`../topics/preview`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:97
msgid "``content_retention``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:98
msgid ""
"Default: ``\"30d\"``. How long the node keeps the content of a task after"
" the task ends. Valid values are 1 to 3650 days written as ``<N>d``, or "
"``forever``. Calls to public capabilities keep their content for 7 days "
"regardless. Set with ``anet retention set``, which asks for confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:103
msgid "``without``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:104
msgid ""
"Default: not set. An array of module names that are switched off. A "
"listed module never starts, and the node handles its absence in the same "
"way as for a module that is not compiled in. Names must be known module "
"names and must not repeat; otherwise the file fails validation with "
"``config_invalid``. The key is edited in ``config.json`` or with ``anet "
"init --without`` (names are added, never removed) and ``anet init "
"--with`` (one name is removed). The control plane, MCP and the local A2A "
"interface have no way to write it. See :doc:`../topics/modules`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:117
msgid "``inbound``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:119
msgid "``inbound.policy``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:120
msgid ""
"Default: ``closed``. Which peers may send tasks. ``closed`` accepts tasks"
" only from peers on the allow list, ``approve`` holds tasks of other "
"peers until an operator approves them, and ``open`` accepts tasks from "
"anyone. Set with ``anet inbound policy``; loosening needs terminal "
"confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:125
msgid ""
"The lists are the files ``peers.allow``, ``peers.trust`` and "
"``peers.deny`` in the data directory. They are managed with ``anet "
"peers``. The queue of tasks that wait for approval holds at most 200 "
"tasks, at most 3 per peer, for 72 hours. These are constants."
msgstr ""

