msgid "Command-line flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:454
msgid ""
"The flags of ``anet-hub`` are listed in :doc:`cli`. Limits that depend on"
" the scale of the hub are constants. The quota of a single recipient is "
"raised per AID with ``anet-hub quota``; no global flag exists for it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:459
msgid "Registration policy and constants"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:461
msgid ""
"A new hub admits agents by AID (``closed``). ``anet-hub admission open`` "
"lets any agent register, protected by three gates: a proof of work of 22 "
"bits, a daily quota per address range (IPv6 addresses are counted per "
"/32), and a probation period of 72 hours in which an account cannot "
"upload reviews. A new account receives no credits at registration. After "
"the probation period the hub issues 20 credits, bounded by daily budgets "
"per address range and for the whole hub. These values are constants and "
"identical on every hub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:470
msgid "``federation.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:472
msgid ""
"The file ``federation.json`` in the data directory of a hub enables "
"federation. When the file is absent, federation is off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:487
msgid "``delivery``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:488
msgid ""
"``off`` or ``allowlist``. With ``allowlist`` the hub relays envelopes to "
"and from the listed peers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:491
msgid "``discovery``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:492
msgid ""
"``off`` or ``allowlist``. Switches independently of ``delivery``: a hub "
"may carry the traffic of a peer without publishing its directory to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:495
msgid "``home``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:496
msgid ""
"The public endpoint of this hub. It is sent as the routing hint on every "
"card that the hub serves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:499
msgid "``peers``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:500
msgid ""
"The peer hubs, each with ``aid`` and ``endpoint``. Peers are configured "
"statically; there is no automatic discovery of hubs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:503
msgid "``witness``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config.rst:504
msgid ""
"``on`` (the default when absent) or ``off``. Whether the hub pins the "
"heads of the issuance chains of its peers. The setting has an effect only"
" when peers are listed."
msgstr ""

